operator: Howdy-doo, Gardener!
operator: Nasty business we find ourselves in, hey?
operator: But lucky for you, I took the liberty to scope this place out while you meandered your way over.
operator: There seem to be a few more of those seed vaults spread around the facility.
operator: Must be specimens this place was keeping.
operator: As far as I can tell, one of them is a variant of ficus elastica --- in other words, a rubber tree (which is actually a relative of our darling strangler fig) ---
operator: Only this one has been engineered to produce enzymes that process its latex into usable rubber *inside* the plant, instead of requiring refining.
operator: I'd bet the Green Arsenal will make that thing bouncy as a trampoline.
operator: The other seed I've found resembles nothing I've ever seen before.
operator: Halfway plant, halfway animal, a dash of fungus...
operator: Some kind of organic monitoring system, maybe?
operator: Seems to be able to communicate with other entities through a complex mycorrhizal web that spans the complex.
operator: I guess if you need to peek around corners you could try placing one down and giving it a shot with the Pea Shooter.
operator: But I'm glad we're only finding these two now that we're *inside* the facility.
operator: Partridge pea and sacred lotus are at least native to the area, but these two, out there?
operator: Best not to think about at the moment.
operator: For now, they're useful tools that can aid you in your investigation.
operator: Speaking of, would you like to save any progress in your mission?
- Yes
	operator: Saving progress...
	[signal arg="save_signal"]
	operator: Save complete.
	jump save_done
- No
	operator: Roger dodger! I'll be here if you need to save progress in the future.
	jump save_done
label save_done
operator: Oh, before I forget...
operator: There seem to be some documents scattered around the facility.
operator: Maybe they'll help you in your investigation, who knows.
operator: At that, I wish you the best of luck, Gardener.
operator: See you on the flip side!
[signal arg="scene_end_op"]
[end_timeline]